    <h1>THE BLACK GOLD</h1>
    <p class="sub">Heroine-led pan-India crime thriller · <strong>Samyuktha Menon</strong> as a fearless cop vs. a coal-mafia syndicate · Dir. <strong>Yogesh KMC</strong> · Music <strong>Sam C S</strong> · Producer <strong>Razesh Danda</strong> (Hasya Movies × Maganti Pictures) · Inspired by real coal-syndicate events on the Telangana-Maharashtra border · Releasing Telugu / Hindi / Tamil / Malayalam / Kannada</p>
    <div class="meta">
      <span>Home markets: Telangana &amp; Andhra Pradesh</span>
      <span>Window: June-August 2026</span>
      <span>Prepared June 2026</span>
    </div>
  </header>

  <!-- RECOMMENDATION -->
  <div class="card rec">
    <span class="pill p-go">Recommended release</span>
    <div class="big">Friday, 7 August 2026</div>
    <p>It is the only date in the window that pairs a genuinely clear competitive gap with <strong>two back-to-back long weekends</strong> - Bonalu (Sun 9 + public holiday Mon 10 Aug) and Independence Day (Sat 15 Aug) - before Nani's <em>The Paradise</em> seizes screens on 21 Aug. A real-incident female-cop thriller carried by content and word-of-mouth (not raw star power) needs <strong>runway</strong>, and 7 Aug gives roughly two weeks of it, with Independence Day arriving as a ready-made <em>week-2</em> patriotic booster ("the officer who chose law over the gun, this Independence Day").</p>
    <div class="alt">Strong alternative - Friday 14 August: launches directly into the Independence Day long weekend with maximum patriotic-thematic punch, but gives only one clean week before <em>The Paradise</em>.</div>
    <p class="note" style="margin-top:11px">Hard no-go: 3-24 July. Chiranjeevi's ₹200 cr+ <em>Vishwambhara</em> (eyeing 9-10 July) plus Rajinikanth's <em>Jailer 2</em> will swallow screens, shows and the entire media cycle.</p>
  </div>

