  <!-- COMPETITION -->
  <h2>2 · The competitive field, Jun-Aug 2026</h2>
  <div class="twocol grid2">
    <div>
      <p>July is bracketed by two screen-dominating tentpoles - <strong>Vishwambhara</strong> (Chiranjeevi, ₹200 cr+, eyeing 9-10 Jul) and <strong>Jailer 2</strong> (Rajinikanth). August's anchor is <strong>The Paradise</strong> (Nani, 21 Aug), then <em>Bhogi</em> (Sharwanand, 28 Aug) and Ravi Teja's <em>Irumudi</em>.</p>
      <p>That leaves two clean corridors: <strong>late June</strong> (open field, but no holiday and monsoon onset) and <strong>early August (7 Aug)</strong> - after July's giants fade, before <em>The Paradise</em>. Black Gold belongs in the 7 Aug corridor.</p>
    </div>
