        <li><strong>Per-language labels</strong> - host Hindi / Tamil / Malayalam / Kannada cuts on the dominant label in each market for the pan-India push.</li>
      </ul></div>
    <div class="card"><h3>C · Pan-India / Hindi trade (for the Hindi version)</h3>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Komal Nahta</strong> - X <code>@KomalNahta</code> <span class="pill p-v">verified</span> · national trade analyst, "Film Information".</li>
        <li><strong>Taran Adarsh</strong> - Bollywood trade &amp; box-office updates on X; broad Hindi-belt reach.</li>
      </ul></div>
    <div class="card"><h3>D · Reviewers / creator-influencers</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>Telugu YouTube reviewers (e.g. <strong>Thyview</strong>, <strong>Mahidhar Vibes</strong>, <strong>Tupaki Reviews</strong>) - verify current reach before engaging.</li>
        <li>Thematic creators: <strong>true-crime</strong> and <strong>women-empowerment</strong> pages whose audience overlaps the film's hook.</li>
        <li><strong>Cast &amp; Samyuktha's own handles</strong> - she also presents the film; her posts are the highest-trust channel you control.</li>
      </ul></div>
  </div>

  <!-- RISKS -->
  <h2>6 · Risks &amp; what to re-check</h2>
  <div class="card">
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Competitor dates shift constantly.</strong> Re-confirm Vishwambhara, Jailer 2 and The Paradise 4-6 weeks before locking. If any moves into early August, re-run the scoring - the 7 Aug runway is the whole thesis.</li>
      <li><strong>One-week runway risk (14 Aug option).</strong> Only choose 14 Aug if you are confident of a strong opening weekend, since The Paradise reclaims screens on 21 Aug.</li>
      <li><strong>Monsoon.</strong> July-August rain can soften walk-ins; weight pre-booking and digital conviction (trailer + reviews) accordingly.</li>
      <li><strong>"Real events" sensitivity.</strong> A coal-syndicate-and-CM storyline can invite legal/political pushback - keep disclaimers tight and let the controversy work <em>as</em> buzz, carefully.</li>
      <li><strong>Influencer authenticity.</strong> Favour genuine access over paid praise; audiences and trade punish obviously bought hype, especially for a "message" film.</li>
    </ul>
